==Notes==
* If the player had previously obtained a fighting style but switched to another one, relearning the original one will be free.
* To obtain all fighting styles, it would cost a total of {{Money|25,400,000}} and {{Fragment|31,500}}.
* All fighting styles will keep their [[mastery]] even when the player learns a new one. 
* Using a Fighting Style on [[enemies]] or players that have [[Elemental]] immunity will not damage them.
** Using [[Aura]] bypasses their intangibility.
* Most fighting styles have less range than [[swords]].
* Combat is the only Fighting Style that does not have the [[Destructible Physics]].
* Instinct Breaking moves can be found [[Instinct/Break#Instinct Breakers|here]].

==Trivia==
* All fighting styles have three different moves, except [[Combat]], which has two, and [[Death Step]] and [[Dark Step]], which have four.
** However, the extra moves on the four-skill fighting styles exist mainly to boost damage of the other abilities. 
* [[Dragon Breath]] is currently the only fighting style having a fragment-only price.
* [[Sanguine Art]] is the only fighting style in the game without a "V2".
* [[Godhuman]] and [[Sanguine Art]] are the only fighting styles that require [[materials]].
* On each fighting style other than [[Combat]], there is the letter M at the bottom left corner of their icon, along with a white or black border surrounding the icon.
** This most likely stands for Melee, the [[Stats|Stat]] that Fighting Styles scale with.

